1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,599
An invoice is disputed. Before calculating, we need to know which contract price applies.

2
00:00:06,599 --> 00:00:11,913
Prooflane helps accounts payable teams trace that decision and hand another reviewer

3
00:00:11,913 --> 00:00:17,670
a case they can reproduce. Here is the actual application running on Vultr.

4
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:22,882
We load an invoice CSV and a separate contract CSV.

5
00:00:22,882 --> 00:00:26,628
Invoice five hundred and four has two overlapping agreements.

6
00:00:26,628 --> 00:00:30,790
We compare their consequences and explicitly select C two R.

7
00:00:30,790 --> 00:00:36,201
Another invoice has no active supplied contract. We exclude it with a reason.

8
00:00:36,201 --> 00:00:39,530
Seven of eight rows are now in scope;

9
00:00:39,530 --> 00:00:42,860
the excluded amount is not counted as savings.

10
00:00:45,909 --> 00:00:50,096
Now we create the baseline in Vultr agent mode.

11
00:00:50,096 --> 00:00:56,143
Serverless Inference writes Python, and the Vultr virtual machine dispatches it to a

12
00:00:56,143 --> 00:01:00,795
disposable Docker container. An independent Decimal checker verifies every finding.

13
00:01:00,795 --> 00:01:07,308
The completed result is seven hundred and sixty eight dollars of positive price variance,

14
00:01:07,308 --> 00:01:10,099
with five rows flagged for review.

15
00:01:11,909 --> 00:01:17,522
The result stays connected to its sources. Selecting an invoice reveals the exact quantity

16
00:01:17,522 --> 00:01:22,334
and both prices. One contract price, C one, affects three invoices together.

17
00:01:22,334 --> 00:01:26,744
The assumptions view calculates the cent at which review priority changes:

18
00:01:26,744 --> 00:01:30,353
eighty two dollars and sixty cents creates a tie.

19
00:01:30,353 --> 00:01:33,961
One cent more makes a different invoice the priority.

20
00:01:33,961 --> 00:01:37,169
These are explicit what if calculations, not predictions.

21
00:01:40,013 --> 00:01:45,853
In Proof, we can inspect the actual model, the generation and explanation request identifiers,

22
00:01:45,853 --> 00:01:51,692
and the Python that ran. Vultr selects the focus of the guidance after verification;

23
00:01:51,692 --> 00:01:57,949
the server inserts the checked amounts. Execution has no network, no host mounts or injected

24
00:01:57,949 --> 00:02:01,703
credentials, a read only root filesystem, and resource limits.

25
00:02:01,703 --> 00:02:04,623
The container is removed after the task.

26
00:02:05,673 --> 00:02:11,142
Let us test containment from the site. A fresh container runs the probes now.

27
00:02:11,142 --> 00:02:16,610
Network access fails, writing to the root filesystem is denied, the inference key variable

28
00:02:16,610 --> 00:02:19,735
is absent, and the process is not root.

29
00:02:19,735 --> 00:02:23,251
Finally, the system confirms that the container was removed.

30
00:02:23,251 --> 00:02:29,110
These five observed checks pass; they are evidence of these controls, not a claim that

31
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:31,063
every possible escape is impossible.

32
00:02:36,354 --> 00:02:39,848
We download the case packet and verify it again.

33
00:02:39,848 --> 00:02:44,118
The verifier reconstructs the source choices, arithmetic, receipt links and priority

34
00:02:44,118 --> 00:02:49,553
boundaries. All seven groups pass. The same packet can be checked offline without our

35
00:02:49,553 --> 00:02:55,764
server. Its hashes detect changes; they do not prove that a supplier or contract is authentic.

36
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:09,721
Prooflane turns a disputed amount into a review another colleague can reproduce.

37
00:03:09,721 --> 00:03:14,147
Our initial users are accounts payable and procurement teams.

38
00:03:14,147 --> 00:03:20,540
A team subscription is a business hypothesis; customer savings have not been measured.

39
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:25,458
Try the public demo and inspect the open source repository.

40
00:03:25,458 --> 00:03:28,900
Built on Vultr. Narration generated with ElevenLabs.
